<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Bongaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1667">1667</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makassar-war">Makassar War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Bongaya was signed in November 1667 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-hasanuddin">Sultan Hasanuddin</a> of Gowa and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>, whose commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornelis-speelman">Cornelis Speelman</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arung-palakka">Arung Palakka</a> of Bone, had defeated Makassar. Gowa had to expel other Europeans, give the Company a trade monopoly and cede forts, including Ujung Pandang, renamed Fort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rotterdam">Rotterdam</a>. Fighting resumed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somba-opu">Somba Opu</a> fell in 1669.</p></div>
